# Lagrangian field theory: the formulation of physics by a Lagrangian, a single function whose integral the actual
# history of a system makes stationary (the principle of least action). The field equations follow from it, and every
# symmetry of the Lagrangian gives a conserved quantity (Noether's theorem). It is how the Standard Model is written.
# This note marks the action principle as the organizing law of field theory.
